Just for clarification, if you then wear a positively-enchanted
HoB or GoD, does that bring your total even higher, or does
it stay capped at 25?  If the latter (which seems more likely),
does removing said item then bring your max back down by
the item's enchantment, or does your naked max stay 25?

[Runs off to test in wizmode...]

Answer:  if your naked attribute scores are 25 and you
then don positively-enchanted armor that would ordinarily
improve them, they don't go above 25; but when you take
off said armor, they don't drop below where they were;
your naked max is still 23 or 25 or whatever it was.

Additionally, even if your stats are significantly below
maximum, having a negatively-enchanted stat-boosting
piece of armor stolen while you're putting it on goes
ahead and increases your maximum, as well as your
current stat, right away.  Even if your stats only get
boosted to 16 or so at the time, subsequent quaffing
of blessed potions of gain ability will be able to raise
them above your race's normal maximum.

I assume the same thing happens in reverse with
positively enchanted armor.  Say, for instance, that
you're human (so normal max would be 18) and
have got the stat in question up to 11, then due
to this bug and +2 armor it gets cut back to 9.
Your max would then be 16, I think.

Fascinating.

Moral:  do not attempt to don positively-enchanted
stat-boosting armor in the immediate vicinity of a
nymph if you are currently wearing other armor.
That's fairly counterintuitive -- normally you want
to get all your armor back on as fast as possible
after it gets charmed off.


